# Overview

This room introduces the **AWS Shared Responsibility Model** and explains how security responsibilities are divided between AWS and its customers.

AWS secures the cloud platform and services to a certain extent, while what you build on top is your responsibility to secure.

The room also examines real-world cloud security incidents to demonstrate how exposed credentials, overly permissive IAM policies, and misconfigured storage can lead to data exposure.

---

# Task 1 - Introduction

AWS secures the cloud platform and services to a certain extent, while what you build on top is your responsibility to secure.

**Key takeaway:** Security in the cloud is a shared responsibility. Using AWS does not automatically make applications, identities, or data secure.

